/**
 * Short summary text of every talent of Nacidos de la bruma, one sentence per talent, taken from the line each talent has in the book's
 * tree diagrams: the metalborn paths (L.137, 143, 147, 151, 157 / PDF 143, 149, 153, 157, 163), the kandra and sangre koloss trees
 * (L.35 and L.39 / PDF 41 and 45), the heroic specialties and main talents of chapter 4 (L.80-121 / PDF 86-127) and the trees of the
 * alomantic and feruchemical powers (chapter 6, L.174-249 / PDF 180-255).
 * Same role as `src/data/talentSummaries.ts` in Stormlight: the compact card of the talent map reads it through `summaryOf(node, summaries)`
 * (§7.7 #4), and when a talent has no entry the UI falls back to the first sentence of its own `description`.
 *
 * Conventions:
 * - Keyed by the exact talent name, the one the engine compares (§7.7, T03). A name that appears in several trees has ONE entry (rule
 *   «Talentos con nombres duplicados», L.75 / PDF 81), written at its first tree: Investido, Quemar instintivamente, Trazas de metal,
 *   Almacenamiento rápido, Decantación instintiva, Mente de metal integrada and Mentes de metal ampliadas (metalborn paths); Burbuja
 *   ampliada, Burbuja espontánea and Burbuja expeditiva (bendaleo, cadmio); Control de masas, Influencia precisa and Manipulación sutil
 *   (cinc, latón); Prevenirse con palanca (acero, hierro); Reflejos acelerados (feruquimia de acero y de cinc); Precisión de estaño,
 *   Armamento de brazo de peltre and Lanzador de peltre (alomancia and feruquimia); and the names that several heroic specialties share
 *   (Compostura, Torvo, Paso firme, Robusto…). In every case the diagrams print the same effect in all the trees where the name appears.
 * - Texts are short paraphrases of the diagram line, not quotations (same convention as the rest of `src/data/mistborn/`). The card
 *   glyphs that the PDF text layer turns into letters or digits (Oportunidad, Complicación, reacción, 1/2/3 acciones, acción gratuita) are
 *   written out in words, checked against the full entries of T17-T21. Where a diagram line and its full entry say different things the
 *   summary follows the diagram and the entry carries the `notaLibro`: Mezcla metálica (the diagram says «otro poder naciente»; the entry,
 *   L.142 / PDF 148, two of them; T19) and Dilatación temporal (the diagram says 13,5 m; L.186 / PDF 192 gives a range; T17). The one
 *   exception is Ilustración: its diagram card still says «de potencia» (the Stormlight wording) while the entry and the rule say
 *   «Investidas» (L.106 / PDF 112; T21 `notaLibro`), so the summary says «no Investidas».
 * - Complete: every distinct talent name of T17-T21 has an entry, including the 10 specialties that both manuals share (same name and same
 *   talents, L.374 / PDF 380; T21) and the 6 main talents, whose data Mistborn reuses from Stormlight. Their summaries are written again here
 *   from the Mistborn diagrams instead of importing the Stormlight map, which keeps some glyphs as letters or digits («añadir O», «obtener 2
 *   para») and would make this module import eager code. T34a composes `{ ...TALENT_SUMMARIES, ...TALENT_SUMMARIES_MISTBORN }` (§8): the
 *   Mistborn entries win, and the Stormlight ones only matter for names that Mistborn does not have.
 * Only `src/worlds/mistborn.data.ts` (lazy `import()`) loads this module, and it imports nothing (§8, risk 6).
 */
